  "description": "Like-for-like replacement of existing double glazed wooden sash windows, two on the front elevation and one on the rear elevation of the ground floor of the property which is the ground floor flat of 10 Esmond Road W4 1JQ.  The existing wooden double glazed sash windows, while conforming to the character of the windows in the conservation area, are suffering from severe wood deterioration, sash box deterioration, and non-functioning double glazing units.  The windows do not actually open properly and the insulation provided is minimal.  We aim to replace these on a like-for-like basis with new wooden sash windows with double glazed units that will bring the insulation to current standards while conforming to the visual appearance of other sash windows in the road. This will contribute to the Conservation Area by preserving the character of the windows while enhancing their functionality and thermal properties.  We will use RG Windows, who have done the same work on several other houses in Esmond Road including 113 (application 190563HH) and 106 (201178HH) where planning permission was granted for the same procedure.  ",
